---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import GalleryRandom from "../../components/GalleryRandom.astro";

const imagePool = [
  { src: "/images/teachers/milos-natarajasana-400.webp", alt: "Naṭarājāsana" },
  { src: "/images/classes/yoga-utthita-asva-sanchalanasana-400.webp", alt: "Utthita Aśva Sanchalanāsana" },
  { src: "/images/classes/yoga-eka-pada-adho-mukha-svanasana-400.webp", alt: "Eka Pāda Adho Mukha Śvānāsana" },
  { src: "/images/classes/yoga-class-sukhasana-nyana-mudra-400.webp", alt: "Sukhasana Nyāna Mudrā" }
];
---

<BaseLayout lang="en" page="workshops" title="Yoga Workshops">
  <h1>Yoga Workshops</h1>

  <section>
    <h2>Deepening Your Practice</h2>
    <GalleryRandom
      imagePool={imagePool}
      thumbnail="lg"
      class="thumbnail-right"
    />

    <p>
      Workshops at Studio Sun & Sea offer an immersive environment for deeper learning, reflection, refinement, and exploration of postures. These sessions move at a slower, more intentional pace than regular classes, giving time to understand technique, refine movement patterns, and explore alignment and breath with clarity and ease.
    </p>

    <p>
      Each workshop focuses on a specific theme—such as posture foundations, mobility, breathwork, mindful transitions, or seasonal practices. With more time for explanation, demonstration, and personal attention, workshops create room for questions and deeper understanding.
    </p>

    <p>
      Workshops are open to all levels and all body types. Props, variations, and supportive techniques are used to help you feel stable, comfortable, and confident throughout the session. You are encouraged to take personal responsibility for your safety and needs, honoring your practice in the way that suits you.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What to Expect</h2>
    <p>
      Workshops typically include a blend of guided practice, technique breakdowns, hands-on or verbal assists, and time for exploration. The slower pace allows you to integrate new information and build confidence in your movement patterns.
    </p>

    <p>
      Whether you are new to yoga or looking to refine your practice, workshops offer a supportive space for meaningful growth.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
